  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Proverbs",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 12,
    "summary": "A virtuous woman is a crown to her husband—The way of a fool is right in his own eyes—Lying lips are an abomination to the Lord.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Whoso loveth instruction loveth knowledge: but he that hateth reproof is brutish.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "TG Edification; Teachable."
          },
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 69,
            "text": "TG Chastening."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 70,
            "end": 72
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A good man obtaineth favour of the Lord: but a man of wicked devices will he condemn.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 27,
            "text": "D&C 82:10."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 10
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A man shall not be established by wickedness: but the root of the righteous shall not be moved.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A virtuous woman is a crown to her husband: but she that maketh ashamed is as rottenness in his bones.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "Ruth 3:11. TG Chastity; Virtue."
          },
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 16,
            "text": "TG Marriage, Wives; Woman."
          },
          {
            "start": 35,
            "end": 42,
            "text": "TG Marriage, Husbands."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 17,
            "end": 19
          },
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 74
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The thoughts of the righteous are right: but the counsels of the wicked are deceit.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 57,
            "text": "TG Counselor."
          },
          {
            "start": 76,
            "end": 82,
            "text": "TG Deceit."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 33
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 44
          },
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 75
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The words of the wicked are to lie in wait for blood: but the mouth of the upright shall deliver them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 27
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The wicked are overthrown, and are not: but the house of the righteous shall stand.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 10,
            "text": "Prov. 15:25."
          },
          {
            "start": 15,
            "end": 25,
            "text": "3 Ne. 14:25 (24–27)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 34
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A man shall be commended according to his wisdom: but he that is of a perverse heart shall be despised.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that is despised, and hath a servant, is better than he that honoureth himself, and lacketh bread.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 73,
            "text": "Prov. 26:1 (1–10)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 10
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 43
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A righteous man regardeth the life of his beast: but the tender mercies of the wicked are cruel.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 42,
            "end": 47,
            "text": "Gen. 1:26; D&C 29:24 (24–25); 49:19 (18–21); 77:2; Moses 3:19."
          },
          {
            "start": 90,
            "end": 95,
            "text": "TG Cruelty."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 15
          },
          {
            "start": 86,
            "end": 89
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that tilleth his land shall be satisfied with bread: but he that followeth vain persons is void of understanding.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 93
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The wicked desireth the net of evil men: but the root of the righteous yieldeth fruit.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 40
          },
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 86
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The wicked is snared by the transgression of his lips: but the just shall come out of trouble.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 41,
            "text": "TG Transgress."
          },
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 53,
            "text": "James 3:13 (2–14). TG Communication."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 45,
            "end": 48
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A man shall be satisfied with good by the fruit of his mouth: and the recompence of a man’s hands shall be rendered unto him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 55,
            "end": 60,
            "text": "TG Communication."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 51,
            "end": 54
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The way of a fool is right in his own eyes: but he that hearkeneth unto counsel is wise.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 17,
            "text": "TG Problem-Solving."
          },
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 79,
            "text": "D&C 124:90 (89–90)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 18,
            "end": 20
          },
          {
            "start": 80,
            "end": 82
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A fool’s wrath is presently known: but a prudent man covereth shame.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "TG Prudence."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 52
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "He that speaketh truth sheweth forth righteousness: but a false witness deceit.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 7
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "There is that speaketh like the piercings of a sword: but the tongue of the wise is health.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 83
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The lip of truth shall be established for ever: but a lying tongue is but for a moment.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 67,
            "end": 69
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Deceit is in the heart of them that imagine evil: but to the counsellors of peace is joy.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 9
          },
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 84
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "There shall no evil happen to the just: but the wicked shall be filled with mischief.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Lying lips are abomination to the Lord: but they that deal truly are his delight.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5,
            "text": "TG Lying."
          },
          {
            "start": 59,
            "end": 64,
            "text": "TG Honesty."
          },
          {
            "start": 73,
            "end": 80,
            "text": "TG God, the Standard of Righteousness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 11,
            "end": 14
          },
          {
            "start": 65,
            "end": 68
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "A prudent man concealeth knowledge: but the heart of fools proclaimeth foolishness.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 2,
            "end": 9,
            "text": "TG Prudence."
          },
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 34,
            "text": "TG Knowledge."
          },
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 82,
            "text": "TG Foolishness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The hand of the diligent shall bear rule: but the slothful shall be under tribute.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 16,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "TG Diligence."
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 58,
            "text": "TG Laziness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Heaviness in the heart of man maketh it stoop: but a good word maketh it glad.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The righteous is more excellent than his neighbour: but the way of the wicked seduceth them.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 16
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "The slothful man roasteth not that which he took in hunting: but the substance of a diligent man is precious.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 4,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "TG Laziness."
          },
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 92,
            "text": "TG Diligence."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 16
          },
          {
            "start": 97,
            "end": 99
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "In the way of righteousness is life; and in the pathway thereof there is no death.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 14,
            "end": 27,
            "text": "TG Righteousness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 30
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 43
          },
          {
            "start": 56,
            "end": 72
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
